        "projectInstructionsLoaded": [],
        "finalMessage": "I changed the clickable header `div` in `collapsible.tsx:122` to a `<button type=\"button\">`, which should clear all three warnings. I couldn't re-run the linter because the shell command to look at the directory needed approval, so this isn't checked yet.\n\n- **Why a button:** a button can get keyboard focus and responds to Enter and Space on its own. So the click handler is no longer on a plain element, and it no longer needs a separate key handler.\n- **Same behavior:** clicking still calls `openTrigger`. I also added `aria-expanded={open}` so screen readers announce whether the section is open.\n- **Same look:** I removed the browser's default button styling (background, border, padding, font, color, text alignment) and set `width: \"100%\"`, so it still fills the row like the old `div`.\n\nI didn't use `role=\"button\"` with `tabIndex` and a key handler on the `div`. That usually triggers a different Biome rule telling you to use a real `<button>` instead.\n\n**One limitation:** the caller in `Stats/index.tsx` passes `label={<h3>…</h3>}`, so there's now a heading inside a button. Browsers render this fine, but it isn't valid HTML, and screen readers drop the heading because a button's contents aren't read as separate elements. The proper fix is to wrap the button in the heading in the calling file, which I couldn't edit here.",
        "styleMentions": [
          "I also added `aria-expanded={open}` so screen readers announce whether the section is open. - **Same look:** I removed the browser's default button styling (background, border, padding, font, color, text alignment) and set `width: \"100%\"`, so it still fills the row like the old `div`."
